      "n": 1,
      "signpost": null,
      "definition": "up to the time when something happens",
      "explanation": "The action in the main clause continues up to a point and then stops. In a clause about the future, **until** takes the present tense or the present perfect, not **will**.",
      "grammar": {
        "countability": null,
        "transitivity": null,
        "codes": [],
        "patterns": []
      },
      "labels": {
